+ip_forward_ttl_mode - INTEGER
+	Select the IPv4 TTL policy for software forwarding in this network
+	namespace. Valid values are:
+
+	- 0 - Decrement TTL and update the IPv4 header checksum (default).
+	- 1 - Preserve TTL and leave the checksum unchanged by the TTL policy.
+
+	The policy is read for each packet by ordinary IPv4 forwarding,
+	multicast forwarding, IPVS, Netfilter software flowtable forwarding,
+	and nftables IPv4 neighbour forwarding. Existing TTL expiry checks
+	are unchanged; in particular, ordinary forwarding still rejects
+	packets with TTL less than or equal to one in either mode.
+
+	New network namespaces start in mode 0 independently of the creating
+	namespace. Changes affect subsequent software packet processing and
+	do not require a route or software flowtable flush. Packets already
+	being processed may use the previous setting.
+
+	This does not change IPv6 Hop Limit, locally generated packet TTL,
+	or hardware, BPF, or vendor forwarding paths that bypass these hooks.
+	Other packet rewriting rules may still change TTL or the checksum.
+
+	With CONFIG_IP_FORWARD_TTL_PUBLIC_CONTROL, /proc/ttl_ctl provides
+	an unprivileged alias for this value. Each open descriptor pins the
+	opener's network namespace; the sysctl's own permissions are unchanged.
+
+	Default: 0
+
